OL,3,AChannel 4 documentary and journalists
OL,4,A'poisoned the well' against Russell
OL,5,ABrand, court hears
OL,6,
OL,7,FJournalists "poisoned the well of
OL,8,Fjustice" by prompting complainants to
OL,9,Fcome forward and make criminal
OL,10,Fallegations against Russell Brand,
OL,11,Fjurors have heard.
OL,13,FIn his closing speech on Monday, Ian
OL,14,FWinter KC, Brand's defence barrister,
OL,15,Fsaid a Channel 4 documentary and
OL,16,Fstories in the Times and Sunday Times
OL,17,Fthat made allegations about Brand in
OL,18,F2023 "caused people who had not
OL,19,Fpreviously considered for it to be
OL,20,Fappropriate to bring criminal
OL,21,Fallegations against him, to do so, and
OL,22,Fvery many years after."
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG9/18
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
